# Copy to `.env`. SERIAL_PORT is where the Pi hears the receiver board.
#
# The receiver is wired to the Pi's serial pins (header pins 8 and 10), which
# are /dev/serial0 once the port is switched on: README, "Prepare the Pi".
#
# A receiver plugged into a USB port instead shows up under
#   ls -l /dev/serial/by-id/
# Use that full path: it survives reboots and re-plugs, unlike /dev/ttyACM0
# or /dev/ttyUSB0, which can shuffle.
SERIAL_PORT=/dev/serial0

# Where the PWA repo is checked out. Only needed if it isn't next to this
# folder as ../central_node_pwa.
# PWA_DIR=../central_node_pwa
